    "reason": "The assertion that brain astrocyte networks utilize the lactate shuttle mechanism to transfer metabolic fuel to neurons is well-established in neuroscience. The 'astrocyte-neuron lactate shuttle' hypothesis, supported by extensive evidence (e.g., Pellerin & Magistretti, 1994), posits that astrocytes produce lactate from glucose and transfer it to neurons for oxidative metabolism during periods of high activity. No substantive flaw or counterexample exists; the claim accurately reflects current scientific consensus.",
